= Applications to Function Theory \ and Algebraic Geometry <ch:applications>

#source(117)
In the two previous chapters we have emphasized the systematic investigation of
properties of residues with respect to holomorphic mappings using some facts of
algebraic topology (homology theory) and function theory (elementary properties
of analytic sets). In turn, the results we have obtained about residues can be
applied in certain sections of function theory (to the integral representation
of holomorphic functions and the investigation of holomorphic functions on
analytic sets) and algebraic geometry (to problems on ideals in a polynomial
ring and the theory of intersection). In this chapter we shall present these
applications.
